min":false},"body":"Isn't part of the idea that if the user has a surround system, but stereo override is set, the audio will be computed and output as if the user had stereo speakers?\nIn this case it's not a mere case of channels being muted, but the whole algorithm changing, I think?\n\nMaybe something like:\n\n```suggestion\n\t\t\tIf the specified mode has fewer channels than the system's audio driver, remaining channels will not receive any audio.\n\t\t\tIf the specified mode has more channels than the system's audio driver, the superfluous channels will be discarded.\n```","created_at":"2026-02-10T21:46:09Z","updated_at":"2026-02-10T21:46:44Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105934#discussion_r2790446424","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105934","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2790446424"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105934#discussion_r2790446424"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105934"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2790446424/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":466,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":6,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2806413277","pull_request_review_id":3800016317,"id":2806413277,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc6nRnfd","diff_hunk":"@@ -224,6 +224,8 @@ class AudioServer : public Object {\n \tint channel_count = 0;\n \tint to_mix = 0;\n \n+\tint speaker_mode_config = -1;","path":"servers/audio/audio_server.h","commit_id":"b574e75951bf6cc330c76455fae38e884b5a3fdf","original_commit_id":"b574e75951bf6cc330c76455fae38e884b5a3fdf","user":{"login":"BuzzL